UID:53861-1794337200-1794337200@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Tracing the History of the Upper Beach
DESCRIPTION:Beaches Realtor Mark Battenberg invites you to an evening of discovery as he traces the wonderful history of the Upper Beach. From the decline of the great glaciers to the First Nations People\, The Kingston Road during the war of 1812\, and on to the villages of Norway an Benlamond\, which were the cornerstones of the upper Beach\, as it grew along The Kings Highway in the mid 1800’s. Discover Coleman’s Corners in Little York\, the founding of East Toronto Village\, and the rise and fall of the mighty Grand Trunk Railroad. Info: markbattenberg@rogers.com\, 647-858-9708
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/tracing-the-history-of-the-upper-beach/
LOCATION:Centre 55\, 97 Main St.\, Toronto
END:VEVENT
