SUMMARY:Radiant Vermin presented by Riot King Art Market
DESCRIPTION:Riot King is back on stage this November with Radiant Vermin by playwright Philip Ridley\, playing November 12th to the 22nd. \nCelebrated indie theatre company Riot King Art Market is back on stage this November with Radiant Vermin by playwright Philip Ridley\, playing November 12th to the 22nd\, 2026 at The Red Sandcastle Theatre in Toronto’s beautiful East End. \nOllie and Jill want to tell you about their dream home. Some of the things they did to get it\, you might find shocking. But they want you to know they did it all for their baby… \nRadiant Vermin is a wickedly comedic satire about a young couple who are offered a way onto the property ladder that may turn out to be too good to be true. Through a whirlwind retelling of everything they’ve done to get their dream home\, Ollie and Jill show us just how far we might go to build a better life for ourselves. Playful\, provocative\, and viciously sharp\, this outrageous dark comedy comments on the housing crisis\, homelessness\, and what it really takes to support a family in today’s world. It will leave Toronto audiences shocked\, thrilled\, and feeling a little more connected to everyone who calls this city home. \nContent Advisory: Strong language\, mature themes\, discussions of violence. \nRun time: 110 minutes no intermission. There will be no re-entry.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/radiant-vermin-presented-by-riot-king-art-market/
LOCATION:Red Sandcastle Theatre\, 922 Queen St E\, Toronto\, M4M 2J5
ORGANIZER;CN="Riot King Art Market":MAILTO:producer@riotking.com
END:VEVENT
